P-4 (spec 017, the night shift; plan.md §10; tasks.md T067): the bash gate's refusal of make plan with a ROOT names
the night shift's route.

What it changes: the refusal's message only, and a comment above it. The rule stays as it is: make plan with a ROOT is
refused to every agent session, in every spelling it refuses today. The message now says that, once plans are on, a
night-shift ops task writes a plan request for its runner, which plans that commit as the plan-only role; otherwise you
run it in your terminal.

Spec IDs: decision 1, FR-014 and FR-015 (plans off until your patches merge), research.md R-06.

Needed for: plan on.

How to apply, on your own branch, from the repository's root (one line each):
  B=feat/017-g5-patches
  F=docs/merge-requests/2026-11-12-feat-017-p4.patch
  git show "refs/heads/$B:$F" > /tmp/p4.patch
  sha256sum /tmp/p4.patch
  patch -p1 --dry-run < /tmp/p4.patch
  patch -p1 < /tmp/p4.patch

Verified on a fresh `git archive refs/heads/main` export (main d4870ec8): dry run and apply clean; bash -n and
shellcheck -x clean; the hook, fed the payload of "make plan ROOT=account", exits 2 with the new route in its message.
No test or matrix row matches the message's text (searched).

